2026-09-09T09:30Z claude note Reimagine pass only (Fable, read-only, no plan and no edit to this ticket's scope) recorded at conception/0744-reimagining-problem-class-grouping.md. It argues five angles the ticket as filed did not: reruns make a Zotero collection stale the moment it is created; tags dominate collections but a self-maintaining tag set is itself an automatic library write the author ruled against; a document's problem class is the first obstacle found, not a fixed partition, so it can shift on rerun; a saved search cannot express any of these classes without the same tag-maintenance cost; and no comparable system (compilers, ocrmypdf, package resolvers, Zotero's own Duplicate/Unfiled/Retracted views) persists a reason-grouped report as a to-do list rather than recomputing it live. Recommends splitting into a zero-write ticket (carry the reason through inspect(), render per-class with a "show in library pane" selection control instead of a collection) and a second, deferred ticket for any library write (blocked on a ruling; tags, not a collection, if ever). Not acted on here — this ticket's scope is unchanged pending the author's own read of the note.

2026-09-09T10:10Z claude note Two more addenda recorded at the same note, correcting one along the way: the author's actual proposal was "add a button to save problematic references to the clipboard" (an earlier draft of the note misread it as postprocessing the existing journal-copy ring, corrected in place). Assessed as a clean fit -- same proven copySDTText plumbing, reads the same Ticket A grouping, no bounded-cap decision needed since a clipboard export is not constrained to a fixed-height window, and the tone constraint moves downstream once nothing renders inside the plugin's own surface. Second addendum, from "is the information in memory, and how about an API, agents do what they want with it": half yes -- the coarse status is already live in observed, the problem class specifically is not, so carrying it out of inspect() is a prerequisite for every option including this one. Direct precedent exists for the API framing: bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin already runs two endpoints on Zotero's local server, and ticket 0758 (Codex, same day) is already proposing to grow that same plugin into a shared API surface for exactly this kind of consumer-decides-what-to-do data. Flagged as a note for 0758's contract review as much as for this ticket, not a fully separate feature. All three options (dialog grouping, clipboard button, API view) are non-exclusive.

2026-09-09T10:35Z claude note Correction, author's prompt: "Document content API is one at a time." Checked against the actual handler (bootstrap.js:119-162): Status.init only answers for keys the caller already supplies, and with none falls back to a library-wide aggregate with no per-item rows -- it cannot enumerate "every item matching a condition" any more than 0758's per-document content modes can. So a classification view is not a cheap field added to the existing status response as the previous draft said; it is a new enumerate-by-class capability, closer in size to a fourth mode alongside 0758's three than to a query-string tweak. The precedent still argues for where it lives (0758's plugin, not a second one) -- just not for how small it is. Corrected in the note.

