2026-09-09T11:15Z claude note unsupported-pack and inspection-error's remedy text checked against the code rather than guessed, per the author's "reason a wording that is both correct and clear": unsupported-pack is confirmed exactly the author's own guess, a packVersion/schemaVersion mismatch against the running Zotero's own declared versions (bootstrap.js:1977-1988), self-correcting on the next inspection once a compatible pack replaces it, which per the plugin's own About text happens the next time a Zotero feature needs the attachment's text -- the remedy names that moment. inspection-error is scheduler.js's own catch-all for any exception inspect() throws; no single cause, so no single remedy sentence -- the caught error string already survives per item in observed, so the correct and clear treatment is showing it per item rather than inventing one sentence that would misdescribe most of its members. Body's Actions/Test/Verification/Invariants/Exit-criteria rewritten to match the ruling; three Open items recorded as blocking implementation (sync-state discriminator unverified, no-text-layer measurement not taken, "No attachment" scan not sized) rather than guessed past.

