2026-09-09T13:47Z MinhHaDuong note Final two rulings, taken one at a time. Section name: "Not indexed" -- drops "attachments," which disagreed with its own "No attachment" subsection. Multi-library selection: asked to discuss cause-primary (the design as built) against a structural pivot to library-primary before ruling -- library-primary would solve button-scoping for free but breaks the design's own settled repair-based principle for no gain in the common single-library case, and scatters each cause's size and remedy text across parallel subtrees in the measured multi-library case. Kept cause-primary; where a cause's members span more than one library, the subsection splits at the row (title list + both buttons per library), not at the top level, so the remedy sentence is still stated once. No open design decisions remain; Actions/Test/Verification/Exit-criteria updated accordingly.

