2026-09-10T09:58Z claude note RULED by the author: remove the per-subsection "Export list to clipboard" and fold the identifiers into the journal report. His ground was that a shown-in-library selection is one keystroke from the clipboard. Reading the code first changed the argument without changing the verdict -- the two controls do not produce the same artifact (the export was title+library:key, Zotero's quick copy is a citation) and they act on different sets by design (displayed membership vs. surviving items). What carries the removal is the other reason: the pair rendered once per library subsection per class, and a library:key column is a developer's artifact standing in a layer written under a plain-language constraint. Implemented as identifiers only, never titles, which makes the fold NARROWER than the button it replaces and keeps SPEC.md's R22 rule intact -- that paragraph already admits the key pair as a record field and already refuses titles at every sink. Uncapped: a class with four thousand members serializes four thousand keys, because a truncated membership answers a different question. Ticket 0716 landed in the same change, since the paragraph that had to describe the new payload is the paragraph 0716 asked to be written.

--- body ---
## Purpose and authority

Implement the sitter's repair-oriented Details view specified in SPEC.md
§5.2.7. The author's accepted design review is recorded in DECISIONS.md
(2026-09-09). That specification owns the class table, explanatory text,
publication contract and controls. Earlier logs and
conception/0744-reimagining-problem-class-grouping.md describe the design's
history; they do not override the corrected contract.

## Review consequences

- `missing-source` currently includes every `IOUtils.stat` exception, not
  just absence. `attachmentLinkMode` identifies storage mode but cannot prove
  that sync will restore a file. Preserve a safe access-error reason and
  distinguish confirmed absence before applying the display mapping.
- The scheduler catches inspection exceptions and stores `String(error)`.
  Capture a validated class before discarding the exception, together with
  whatever safe identity is available. `getAsync` itself can fail, so neither
  a title nor `attachmentFilename` is guaranteed. Keep the input item ID as
  the final fallback; do not perform an unguarded second metadata lookup.
- The early-page external extraction reported in prior discussion does not
  prove absence of text throughout a source or native pack. Ticket 0760
  establishes the native-pack content contract; no OCR diagnosis is inferred.
- Pack version and schema major version are independent dimensions. The
  display comparison needs mixed/unknown cases. Existing code alone does not
  prove automatic regeneration for either direction.
- `observed` is private to the scheduler. Rendering cannot obtain a coherent
  full membership list from the existing count-only snapshot. Publish the
  specified view explicitly, including no-attachment membership and updates.

## Implementation work

- Carry safe identity, descriptive metadata, classification reasons and
  comparable version fields through inspection and scheduler error handling.
- Implement the class mapping from SPEC.md §5.2.7 without altering admission
  behavior; consume 0760's verified-empty result, including its cache path.
- Add the bibliographic-item scan and notification invalidation for old and
  new parents, trash/restore, reparenting and attachment creation/deletion.
  Use the existing reconciliation schedule, not a new dialog polling loop.
- Publish coherent immutable memberships with the completed census and
  incremental updates. Avoid copying full memberships at every scan tick.
- Render the section, per-library rows, complete-membership actions and
  incremental expansion. Reuse clipboard success and failure feedback.
- Add all strings to SDT_TEXT and the new UI site to the vocabulary guard.
  Have the author review the actual rendered tone.

## Verification

- [ ] Every specified class is exercised, including opposite/malformed
      version dimensions and reader rejection before version inspection.
- [ ] Missing files and permission/stat failures have different explanations;
      a stored missing file does not imply a remote copy exists.
- [ ] Failure before item lookup, during title lookup and during inspection
      retains a usable fallback; no path or raw message reaches UI or export.
- [ ] Empty, sparse, unknown and cached native content follow 0760's contract.
- [ ] Counts, titles and action membership share one completed generation
      during initial scan, reconciliation, incremental changes and interruption.
- [ ] Attachments added, deleted, reparented, trashed and restored update both
      parents correctly; notes/URL-only attachments do not hide file absence.
- [ ] Multi-library rows, deleted items before a click, unavailable libraries
      and updates during an action follow the specified stale-action behavior.
- [x] The diagnostic report carries the complete not-indexed membership as
      identifiers, grouped by class, and carries no title. Superseded the
      per-subsection export by the author's ruling of 2026-09-10; the escaped
      line break and the visible clipboard failure went with the control, since
      a JSON report escapes its own strings and the journal copy has its own
      failure line.
- [ ] The selection control is inert until activated, includes a tooltip, acts
      beyond the preview cap and does not write library records or initiate
      extraction.
- [ ] Empty groups are hidden; expanding a large list preserves responsiveness,
      focus and expansion through progress updates.
- [ ] Vocabulary checks and author review of rendered tone pass.
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Exit criteria

The corrected SPEC.md §5.2.7 view is implemented and the verification items
above pass. This ticket remains open and depends on 0760; design acceptance
is not implementation acceptance. No API, collection creation or new native
regeneration behavior is included.
